2. RCA Conclusion

Based on the production logs, application flow analysis, Jira isolation evidence, and confirmation from the ASM team, the failure is triggered during Aspose-based processing of the identified EPIC PDF.

The affected PDF 72170-4_1002036770_20250617.pdf contains interactive PDF fields. During PDF processing/merge, Aspose encounters an “An attempt to create annotation using invalid dictionary” error while processing the PDF structure associated with these interactive fields.

The identified PDF is confirmed as the trigger for the issue because removing this PDF from the EPIC ZIP allows the remaining documents to be processed and the final PDF to be generated successfully.

Therefore, the primary cause is the interactive-field/annotation structure in the source PDF being incompatible with the current Aspose PDF processing/merge behavior.

The application-level contributing factor is that the existing exception handling catches the page-level Aspose processing exception, skips the affected resize operation, and continues processing without marking the complete source PDF as failed/excluding it from the subsequent merge. This allows the problematic PDF to continue through the downstream processing path and ultimately causes final PDF generation to fail.

This is much stronger than the current wording because you now have ASM confirmation.

